# Terraform
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
**/terraform.tfvars
**/*.auto.tfvars
**/tfplan
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*

# Credentials — never commit any of these
**/*-key.json
**/service-account*.json
**/application_default_credentials.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Blog HTML (lives in katta698.github.io, kept local only if generated here)
**/docs/blog/*.html

# LinkedIn drafts — personal working files
**/docs/linkedin/

# Build artifacts
**/functions/builds/
**/*.zip

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/

# Local study/prep docs
**/docs/explainer.md
**/docs/blog-prep.md

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Working files for Claude Code — local only, same as the AWS lab
CLAUDE.md
SESSION_CONTEXT.md
SESSION_ARCHIVE.md
BRIEFINGS.md

# Internal setup and design notes. These contain account specifics and working
# reasoning; the public README carries what a reader actually needs.
docs/SETUP.md
docs/CLOUD-IDENTITY-SETUP.md
docs/HIERARCHY.md

# Per-week study material — local only
**/docs/interview-questions.md
**/docs/references.md

# Playwright profile and exported cookies — session credentials, never committed
playwright_profile/
*_cookies.json

# Claude Code local permissions. Personal to this machine and deliberately not
# committed, matching the AWS lab. A shared settings.json in a public repo would
# hand every reader's Claude Code the same auto-approvals — and this one allowed
# `terraform apply` without a prompt, on a repo whose whole point is showing
# people how to run infrastructure carefully.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Rendered card artifacts sit beside their .card source; the PUBLISHED copy
# lives in docs/blog/screenshots/ and is what the blog embeds. Committing both
# stores every figure twice and makes it ambiguous which one a post uses.
week-*/docs/blog/*.png

# Build artifact from data.archive_file.rotator
week-12-secret-management/terraform/.rotator.zip

# Measurement JSON holds full resource names, which embed the project NUMBER.
# The findings they support are published in the figures and the post, with
# identifiers redacted; the raw files stay local.
week-*/docs/*-measurement*.json
week-*/docs/cmek-revocation*.json
